---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SOCIALS } from '../../components/content.js';
// Privacy Policy and Terms of Use in one page. Written from what the code really does (server.js, src/lib/signup.js, public/js/*.js).
// Change the code's data handling -> change this page and its dates. No personal email, address or phone here, ever.
// The contents list numbers itself from these arrays; keep the order in step with the numbered headings below.
const instagram = SOCIALS.find((s) => s.id === 'instagram').href;
const PRIVACY = [
  ['intro', 'Introduction'],
  ['collect', 'Information We Collect'],
  ['use-info', 'How We Use Information'],
  ['disclosure', 'Disclosure of Information'],
  ['third-party', 'Third-Party Services'],
  ['storage', 'Cookies and Local Storage'],
  ['retention', 'Data Retention'],
  ['security', 'Data Security'],
  ['children', 'Children’s Privacy'],
  ['rights', 'Your Rights and Choices'],
  ['dnt', 'Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control'],
  ['privacy-changes', 'Changes to This Policy'],
  ['privacy-contact', 'Contact'],
];
const TERMS = [
  ['acceptance', 'Acceptance of Terms'],
  ['ownership', 'Intellectual Property'],
  ['trademarks', 'Trademarks'],
  ['permitted-use', 'Permitted Use'],
  ['other-sites', 'Third-Party Links and Services'],
  ['shows-terms', 'Events and Releases'],
  ['shop-terms', 'Merchandise'],
  ['health', 'Photosensitivity and Accessibility Notice'],
  ['as-is', 'Disclaimer of Warranties'],
  ['liability', 'Limitation of Liability'],
  ['indemnity', 'Indemnification'],
  ['law', 'Governing Law and Venue'],
  ['severability', 'Severability'],
  ['terms-changes', 'Changes to These Terms'],
  ['contact', 'Contact'],
];
---
<Base title="Privacy and terms | GLucak" description="Privacy Policy and Terms of Use for the GLucak website.">
  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="h-privacy">
    <div class="wrap prose legal-page">
      <h1 id="h-privacy" class="prose-h">Privacy and terms</h1>
      <p class="muted">Effective date: November 18, 2026<br />Last updated: November 18, 2026</p>
      <p>This page contains two documents: the Privacy Policy, which describes how information is collected and used on this website, and the Terms of Use, which govern your use of it. Please read both carefully.</p>

      <nav class="legal-toc" aria-labelledby="h-contents">
        <h2 id="h-contents" class="legal-toc-h">Contents</h2>
        <p><a href="#privacy">Privacy Policy</a></p>
        <ul>{PRIVACY.map(([id, t], i) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{`${i + 1}. ${t}`}</a></li>)}</ul>
        <p><a href="#terms">Terms of Use</a></p>
        <ul>{TERMS.map(([id, t], i) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{`${i + 1}. ${t}`}</a></li>)}</ul>
      </nav>

      <h2 id="privacy">Privacy Policy</h2>

      <h3 id="intro">1. Introduction</h3>
      <p>1.1 This Privacy Policy applies to the website at which it is published (the “Site”). The Site is operated by GLucak, a musical artist based in Pennsylvania, USA (“GLucak”, “we”, “us” or “our”). Mishtuk Web Design builds and looks after the Site on behalf of GLucak.</p>
      <p>1.2 In this Privacy Policy, “you” or “User” means any person who visits or uses the Site. This Privacy Policy describes the information we collect, how we use it and the choices available to you.</p>
      <p>1.3 We do not sell, rent or trade personal information. The Site does not display advertising and does not use tracking technologies.</p>

      <h3 id="collect">2. Information We Collect</h3>
      <p>2.1 <strong>Information you provide.</strong> The Site may be used in full without identifying yourself, and there are no user accounts for visitors. The only personal information you may provide to us through the Site is your email address, if you choose to join the email list by entering it and pressing Join.</p>
      <p>2.2 <strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> As with any website, when your device requests a page, basic technical information is transmitted, such as your IP address and browser type. This information is processed as described in Section 2.3 and Section 7.</p>
      <p>2.3 <strong>Server logs.</strong> The company that hosts the Site may keep standard request logs, which may include IP address, date and time, the page requested and browser type. Our own server records errors and sign-ins to the private editing area used by the Site’s team. A record of a failed sign-in includes the IP address and the name entered.</p>
      <p>2.4 <strong>Information we do not collect.</strong> We do not use analytics, advertising, tracking pixels or device fingerprinting. The Site has no contact form. The shop is currently a preview only; no item can be purchased and the shop collects no information.</p>

      <h3 id="use-info">3. How We Use Information</h3>
      <p>3.1 We use your email address solely to send you news about shows and new music.</p>
      <p>3.2 We use technical information and logs solely to operate the Site, diagnose errors and protect the Site against abuse.</p>
      <p>3.3 To prevent spam and repeated sign-in attempts, the Site counts attempts per IP address over a period of a few minutes. These counts are held only in the server’s memory and are not saved.</p>

      <h3 id="disclosure">4. Disclosure of Information</h3>
      <p>4.1 <strong>Email service.</strong> When you join the email list, your email address is sent from our server to Kit, our email service provider, which stores the list and sends the emails. Your browser does not communicate with Kit directly when you sign up. Kit may record whether an email was opened or a link was clicked, in accordance with the <a href="https://kit.com/privacy">Kit privacy policy</a>.</p>
      <p>4.2 <strong>Hosting.</strong> The company that hosts the Site processes requests to the Site and may keep the logs described in Section 2.3.</p>
      <p>4.3 We do not otherwise sell, rent, trade or share your personal information with third parties.</p>

      <h3 id="third-party">5. Third-Party Services</h3>
      <p>5.1 The Site embeds and links to services operated by third parties (“Third-Party Services”). Each Third-Party Service is governed by its own terms and privacy policy, and we do not control the information it collects.</p>
      <p>5.2 <strong>Spotify.</strong> The playlist player on the Home and Music pages loads from Spotify as you scroll to it. The player for an individual release on the Music page loads only after you press it. See the <a href="https://www.spotify.com/us/legal/privacy-policy/">Spotify privacy policy</a>.</p>
      <p>5.3 <strong>YouTube.</strong> Videos load from YouTube’s privacy-enhanced service (youtube-nocookie.com), and only after you press Play. Until then, the preview image is served from our own server. See the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a>.</p>
      <p>5.4 <strong>External links.</strong> Links to Instagram, Threads, X, YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music, Bandsintown, SoundCloud, Patreon and music stores open those sites, which have their own policies. Requests to book a show are made through GLucak’s Instagram; anything you send there is handled by Instagram under its own policy, and we use it only to reply to you.</p>
      <p>5.5 Once a player loads or you follow a link, the relevant Third-Party Service may set its own cookies. The Site’s fonts and images are served from our own server, so no other content loads from third parties.</p>

      <h3 id="storage">6. Cookies and Local Storage</h3>
      <p>6.1 The Site sets no cookies for visitors. It stores at most two settings in your browser’s local storage:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>motion</code>: your choice of Motion on or off from the switch in the footer.</li>
        <li><code>palette</code>: a color preview used only by the Site’s owner. Visitors do not normally have this setting.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>6.2 Neither setting identifies you, and neither is sent to us. You may clear them at any time in your browser settings.</p>
      <p>6.3 The private editing area used by the Site’s team uses one sign-in cookie, <code>gl_edit</code>, which is sent only to that area.</p>

      <h3 id="retention">7. Data Retention</h3>
      <p>7.1 Your email address remains on the list until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it.</p>
      <p>7.2 The attempt counts described in Section 3.3 are kept in memory for minutes and are erased when the server restarts.</p>
      <p>7.3 Logs are kept only for as long as needed to operate and protect the Site.</p>

      <h3 id="security">8. Data Security</h3>
      <p>We take reasonable measures to protect the Site and your information, including HTTPS, strict security settings and limits on repeated attempts. No website is completely secure, however, and we cannot guarantee that information will never be lost or accessed without authorization.</p>

      <h3 id="children">9. Children’s Privacy</h3>
      <p>The Site is not directed to children under 13. Consistent with the Children’s Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA), we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has joined the email list, please contact us as described in Section 13 and we will delete the address.</p>

      <h3 id="rights">10. Your Rights and Choices</h3>
      <p>10.1 You may:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>unsubscribe from the email list at any time using the link included in every email;</li>
        <li>ask us what personal information we hold about you, and ask us to correct or delete it; and</li>
        <li>turn off Motion, and clear the Site’s local storage, at any time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>10.2 Residents of California, other US states, the European Union and the United Kingdom may have additional rights under applicable law. We honor these requests regardless of where you live. We may need to verify that a request comes from you before acting on it.</p>

      <h3 id="dnt">11. Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control</h3>
      <p>We do not track Users across websites, and we do not sell or share personal information for advertising. Accordingly, there is no tracking for a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal to disable. We nevertheless honor these signals.</p>

      <h3 id="privacy-changes">12. Changes to This Policy</h3>
      <p>Before the Site begins to use information in any new way, we will update this Privacy Policy and the “Last updated” date at the top of this page.</p>

      <h3 id="privacy-contact">13. Contact</h3>
      <p>Questions and requests about this Privacy Policy may be sent to GLucak by message on <a href={instagram}>Instagram</a>. If you are on the email list, you may also reply to any email from the list.</p>

      <h2 id="terms">Terms of Use</h2>

      <h3 id="acceptance">1. Acceptance of Terms</h3>
      <p>1.1 These Terms of Use (the “Terms”) govern your use of the Site operated by GLucak. Terms defined in the Privacy Policy above have the same meaning in these Terms.</p>
      <p>1.2 By accessing or using the Site, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, you must not use the Site.</p>

      <h3 id="ownership">2. Intellectual Property</h3>
      <p>2.1 The music, videos, photographs, artwork and text on the Site (the “Content”) are owned by GLucak or by the photographers and collaborators credited on each page.</p>
      <p>2.2 Except as permitted in Section 4, you may not copy, download, re-upload, sell, sample, remix or otherwise reproduce the Content, or use it to train artificial intelligence systems, without prior written permission.</p>

      <h3 id="trademarks">3. Trademarks</h3>
      <p>The GLucak name, logos and album art identify the artist. You may not use them in any manner that suggests GLucak made, sells or endorses a product or service that he does not. Other names and logos on the Site belong to their respective owners.</p>

      <h3 id="permitted-use">4. Permitted Use</h3>
      <p>You may listen to, watch and share links to the Content for your own personal, non-commercial use. You agree not to misuse the Site or use it in violation of these Terms or applicable law.</p>

      <h3 id="other-sites">5. Third-Party Links and Services</h3>
      <p>The Site links to and embeds Third-Party Services, such as Spotify, YouTube, Instagram, Bandsintown and Patreon. We are not responsible for their content, policies, prices or availability. Your use of a Third-Party Service is subject to that service’s own terms.</p>

      <h3 id="shows-terms">6. Events and Releases</h3>
      <p>Show dates, times, venues, prices and release dates are subject to change. You should confirm details with the venue or ticket seller before travelling. We are not responsible for changes or cancellations, a venue’s rules or conduct, tickets purchased from third parties, or travel and other costs.</p>

      <h3 id="shop-terms">7. Merchandise</h3>
      <p>The shop is currently a preview, and no item can be purchased. When the shop opens, the Buy button will take you to the store’s own checkout page, where payment is made under that store’s terms and privacy policy. We will not see or store your card details. Descriptions, stock and prices are subject to change.</p>

      <h3 id="health">8. Photosensitivity and Accessibility Notice</h3>
      <p>8.1 The Site contains video, moving images and motion effects. If you have photosensitive epilepsy or are sensitive to motion or flashing light, please use caution.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The Motion switch in the footer turns off the Site’s motion. Your choice is remembered on that device.</li>
        <li>The Site also follows your device’s reduced-motion setting.</li>
        <li>The Site’s own design does not use flashing, and we omit videos known to contain flashing lights.</li>
        <li>Music videos play from YouTube, and third-party music videos may contain flashing. Watch with care, and stop if you feel unwell.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>8.2 GLucak is an epilepsy survivor, and the Site was built with that in mind. This notice is not medical advice. If you have questions about your health, consult a doctor.</p>

      <h3 id="as-is">9. Disclaimer of Warranties</h3>
      <p>We work to keep the Site accurate and available. However, to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Site and the Content are provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including any warranty that the Site will be error-free, uninterrupted or fit for a particular purpose.</p>

      <h3 id="liability">10. Limitation of Liability</h3>
      <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, GLucak and the people who help operate the Site will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss or damage arising from your use of, or inability to use, the Site. Some jurisdictions do not allow these limitations, so some or all of them may not apply to you.</p>

      <h3 id="indemnity">11. Indemnification</h3>
      <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, you agree to indemnify GLucak against any claim, and the resulting costs, arising from your misuse of the Site or your breach of these Terms.</p>

      <h3 id="law">12. Governing Law and Venue</h3>
      <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, USA, without regard to its conflict of law rules.</p>

      <h3 id="severability">13. Severability</h3>
      <p>If any provision of these Terms is held to be unenforceable, the remaining provisions will remain in full force and effect.</p>

      <h3 id="terms-changes">14. Changes to These Terms</h3>
      <p>We may update these Terms from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top of this page identifies the current version. Your continued use of the Site after a change constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.</p>

      <h3 id="contact">15. Contact</h3>
      <p>Questions about these Terms may be sent to GLucak by message on <a href={instagram}>Instagram</a>. If you are on the email list, you may also reply to any email from the list.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
